WEBVTT

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.720
<b>Yo, yo, yonaka ni bakko suru chimi mouryou</b>

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.720
<i>Yo, yo, at midnight evil spirits stalk</i>

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.760
<b>Marude ikaino ichimi routou</b>

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.760
<i>As if they're from another world</i>

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.010
<b>Mitai na rhymer rhyme shini toujou</b>

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.010
<i>Come to rhyme rhymes</i>

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.180
<b>Kikoetarou? Yamini hibiku oto</b>

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.180
<i>Can you hear them? The sounds resonating from the darkness</i>

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.520
<b>Bibitte kyomi nai furi shiyouto</b>

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.520
<i>Scared senseless, but you pretend not to be interested</i>

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.480
<b>Koukishin wa hini hini jyoushou</b>

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.480
<i>Your curiosity grows day by day</i>

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.770
<b>Nara check shini ikou, here we, here we go ya'll!</b>

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.770
<i>So let's go check them out, here we, here we go ya'll</i>

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:42.980
<b>Ayashi ayaushi shima no chimi mouryou</b>

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:42.980
<i>The mysterious and dangerous evil spirits</i>

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:44.650
<b>Tabun jigoku wa manpai</b>

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:44.650
<i>Hell is probably full with evil spirits</i>

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.940
<b>Afure dashita renchuu ga dantai de retsu wo nashite</b>

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.940
<i>Those that can't get in march in a line</i>

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.150
<b>Kono yo ni stand-by</b>

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.150
<i>Waiting on stand-by in this world</i>

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.360
<b>Yatsura no bun basho ga mazu tannai</b>

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.360
<i>There aren't any spaces left for them</i>

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:53.620
<b>Dooride kisetsu towazu atsui hazu</b>

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:53.620
<i>No wonder, no matter what the season is, it's always hot</i>

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:56.240
<b>Aete heat up sasu ikatsui verse wo</b>

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:56.240
<i>Purposely heating you up with hot verses</i>

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:57.950
<b>Kamashite ase kakasuzo</b>

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:57.950
<i>That make you sweat</i>

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.710
<b>Douse yakedaro kikasena gasshou wo yo!</b>

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.710
<i>You might as well let us hear you all sing!</i>

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:02.790
<b>HA! Koitsuwa marude kajiba</b>

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:02.790
<i>HA! It's just like a scene of a fire</i>

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.170
<b>Sugee nekki tamacchimau shimaguni</b>

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.170
<i>The excitement in the air heats up this island country</i>

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.300
<b>DANGER! Masu masu agacchimau COME ON!</b>

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.300
<i>DANGER! The tension keeps building COME ON!</i>

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.550
<b>(Kono Jipangu mouchoi de panku!)</b>

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.550
<i>(This Japan is about to explode!)</i>

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.680
<b>HA! Koitsuwa marude kajiba</b>

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.680
<i>HA! It's just like a scene of a fire</i>

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.970
<b>Sugee nekki tamacchimau shimaguni</b>

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.970
<i>The excitement in the air heats up this island country</i>

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.180
<b>DANGER! Masu masu agacchimau COME ON!</b>

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.180
<i>DANGER! The tension keeps building COME ON!</i>

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.390
<b>(Kono Jipangu mouchoi de panku!)</b>

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.390
<i>(This Japan is about to explode!)</i>

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.190
My name was
Tsuruya Nanboku the Fourth.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:36.620
The fictional drama I wrote,
Tokaido Yotsuya Kaidan,

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:40.540
is finally coming to an end.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:56.300
I curse you, lemon!

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:01.140
Final Act

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:31.960
Hello. Has a hawk
flown by this way?

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.130
As a matter of fact,
it's right here.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:41.470
If it belongs to you,
then go ahead and take it home.

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:42.980
I appreciate it.

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:46.940
But I'm afraid I may get lost
if I make my way now,

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:49.150
as darkness is approaching.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.490
It can't be that dark outside.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:53.320
Look.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.280
How full the moon is tonight.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:57.450
It's Tanabata.

00:02:58.160 --> 00:02:59.620
Yes, of course.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.790
So, tonight is Tanabata.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:05.790
Well, my lodgings are humble
and I have little to offer.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.580
But you're more than
welcome to stay.

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:39.410
What would a respectable samurai
want with a country girl like me?

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.330
I'm a ronin now.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.120
Moreover, I am bereaved.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.870
Oh. What happened to your wife?

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.170
There was trouble,
and she died in the end.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.840
You're very beautiful.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.430
Please don't toy with my feelings.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:03.310
May I ask your name?

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.270
Tamiya lemon.

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:07.020
And what is your name?

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:08.350
Yes, well...

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:09.940
My name is...

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:22.450
The current flows across the rocks,
then is divided by a waterfall,

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:25.370
yet there is always a place
where the waters meet again.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:26.870
Tamiya!

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.500
Where are you?

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:31.330
Have you found the hawk?

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:41.180
That's strange.
A light in an abandoned shack?

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.030
''Across the rocks...''

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.490
Your name?

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:11.960
It's Iwa.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.590
Oiwa...

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:24.800
I curse you, lemon!

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.400
We'll go to hell together.

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:41.490
Come with me, Tamiya!

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:58.710
lemon!

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:00.920
Are you all right?
Get a hold of yourself!

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:01.970
Mother!

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:08.310
What is it, son?

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:09.140
Damn.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:11.180
I won't let that curse kill me.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.740
The six o'clock bell
has already rung.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:24.490
It's always at this hour
that lemon is ridden with fever.

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:32.660
A dream...

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:34.540
I was only dreaming of Tanabata.

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:45.300
Oiwa!

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:50.310
That child...

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:52.890
I'll take care of him.

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:56.150
So, please!
Rest in peace, Oiwa!

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:05.200
Damn it!

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:09.200
I only married Oume
to win the trust of the Ito family,

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.830
to gain favor with the Kira clan.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:14.410
I am a loyal man!

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:17.380
You're responsible for the deaths
of Oume and Ito Kihei.

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:19.590
They died because of your curse!

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:22.920
I am not to blame!

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:26.380
Damn!

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:30.970
Damn!

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:35.140
Hey, Tamiya!

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:36.480
Get a hold of yourself!

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:45.740
You've completely
fallen under the curse.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:48.700
Chobei, remember the
promise I made?

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:51.490
I'm not counting on it anymore.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:06.590
What are you doing?

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:09.800
Boarding up a rat hole over here.

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:15.810
I've decided not
to see you anymore.

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.440
That's what I came to tell you.

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:18.440
I see.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:14.080
Genshirou.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:15.410
Where's my son?

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:17.120
lemon has gone outside.

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:18.410
Okuma.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:20.080
After separating from me

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.290
I heard you went to serve
under the Kira clan.

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:23.960
That's right.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:27.840
While knowing that I serve under
Asano-Takumi-no-Kami!

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:30.420
As we've separated,
it's none of your concern.

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:33.760
Father.

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:36.180
lemon.

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:37.720
I've heard the rumors.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:40.350
Is it true that you killed Oiwa?

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:46.070
The people I killed were Ito Kihei
and his granddaughter Oume.

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:50.030
What reason did you have
to kill those two?

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:51.200
It was...

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:54.450
It was Oiwa's curse
that forced me to!

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:02.960
lemon.

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:05.380
I'm disowning you.

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:09.800
I understand.

00:10:16.430 --> 00:10:17.850
My son...

00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:22.430
Don't let what Genshirou said
bother you too much.

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:53.800
Damn!

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:55.590
Damn it!

00:10:58.220 --> 00:10:59.260
lemon!

00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:02.890
Mother!

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:22.410
Father!

00:11:33.260 --> 00:11:34.300
Chobei!

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:59.240
I came for Osode's sister Oiwa
and their father Yotsuya Samon!

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:01.450
I, Yomoshichi Satou,
shall seek revenge!

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:03.290
So that's it.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:05.330
Get out of the way, Yomoshichi!

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.070
Damn!

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:50.920
You bastard, Yomoshichi.

00:13:20.990 --> 00:13:25.870
This was the ending to the version
of Tokaido Yotsuya Kaidan

00:13:25.910 --> 00:13:29.870
that was shown at Nakamuraza,
in the 8th year of the Bunsei period.

00:13:30.290 --> 00:13:33.500
Yes. In the script
that I'd originally written,

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:36.460
I revealed lemon's final demise,

00:13:36.550 --> 00:13:40.880
but not whether Oiwa's spirit
had ever entered Nirvana.

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:59.610
<b>Theater Museum of Waseda University</b>

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:45.100
The following year, the 9th of Bunsei,

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:48.520
the story was renamed
<i>Irohagana Yotsuya Kaidan</i>

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:52.270
and the tale was staged once again,
this time in Osaka.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:58.730
But it had been rewritten that
Oiwa's spirit entered Nirvana in the end.

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:02.450
And then in the 12th year of Bunsei,

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:06.240
I, Tsuruya Nanboku the Fourth,
was said to have died.

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:09.200
Those involved with the staging
of Tokaido Yotsuya Kaidan,

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:13.540
including myself, my son,
and my daughter-in-law,

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:16.040
up to 11 members of the production,

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:19.300
had left the world
within a span of 5 years.

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:24.590
So then, who is narrating this story?

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:27.850
That will be explained a little later.

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:39.690
<b>Theater Museum of Waseda University</b>

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:34.270
The Yotsuya Kaidan performances

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:38.440
continued to sell out every time
it was staged, even after my death.

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:42.820
However, many among the actors
and stagehands sustained injuries.

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:46.530
Thus began the rumor that anyone
who didn't go to Oiwa's shrine

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:49.740
<b>Lantern contraption</b>

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:49.030
to get her blessing would be cursed.

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:53.000
There were many contraptions
used in the play,

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:53.250
<b>Altar contraption</b>

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:55.670
and these were probably
to blame for the many injuries.

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:56.670
<b>Wall contraption</b>

00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:59.380
Yotsuya Kaidan
was not only a play,

00:14:59.380 --> 00:15:02.380
but was also adapted
into a popular storytelling format.

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:08.680
<b>Mask used by Ichiryuusai Teizan</b>

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:05.180
Ichiryuusai Teizan the 7th,

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:08.510
became famous for narrating
the tale before the war broke out.

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:10.970
It is said that strange occurrences
were not so rare, such as

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:15.940
<b>1995, May issue of Geijutsu Shincho publication
filmed by Naohiro Tsutsuguchi

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:14.640
a lantern with his name on it falling near the stage without the wind.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:17.650
He died in agony during
the 41st year of the Showa period.

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:22.860
It is said that he muttered ''Lady Oiwa''
with his dying breath.

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:27.280
Once the movie era arrived,

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:30.580
Yotsuya Kaidan
was adapted to film many times.

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:32.120
In the 13th year of Showa,

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:37.210
on the second day of shooting
''Kaidan Oiwa Yakusha''

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:42.090
the director suddenly died,
and a replacement was brought in.

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:45.720
Since then, performers have always
been plagued with such things as

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:47.720
swelling of the face
and injuries to legs.

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:51.680
It is generally believed that
Oiwa's curse still exists,

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:54.850
affecting those that dare
to perform her tale.

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:04.280
Does this curse still exist
in the present?

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:10.030
About 10 years ago, Yotsuya Kaidan
was staged in Shibuya

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:12.080
and was generously received.

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:15.450
But during one of the performances
the producer committed suicide

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:16.910
by jumping off a building.

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:22.880
It has been 180 years
since I wrote this fiction.

00:16:23.050 --> 00:16:25.090
Even with so many years
having passed,

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:29.300
could it be possible
that Oiwa's curse lives on?

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:33.600
I, Tsuruya Nanboku the Fourth,

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:37.020
continue to exist through
the story and the curse

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:39.390
of Yotsuya Kaidan
even though I am dead.

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:44.610
In the 12th year of the Taisho period,

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:49.570
I was said to have paid a visit to
the novelist Akutagawa Ryunosuke.

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:06.000
Tsuruya Nanboku

00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:16.640
I mentioned before that my tale,
Tokaido Yotsuya Kaidan,

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:23.520
was based on popular folklore and
rumors that were told at the time.

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:26.780
Stricken by small pox,

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:29.530
betrayed by her husband,
and turning into a vengeful spirit,

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.780
Oiwa brought great misfortune.

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:35.200
Oiwa was also an example
of a virtuous woman.

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:41.500
There are many other tales
featuring a character named Oiwa.

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:44.960
Even though
Tokaido Yotsuya Kaidan

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:46.880
is said to have been
based on truth,

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:50.630
the story and the characters,
Oiwa and lemon,

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:54.640
were created by me,
and exist solely within my story.

00:17:54.930 --> 00:17:57.140
If such a curse truly exists,

00:17:57.180 --> 00:18:00.890
does it originate from the historical
Oiwa that actually lived?

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:04.650
The curse that has lasted
all these years

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:08.110
only surfaces when
the tale of Yotsuya Kaidan

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:11.700
is being retold and brought to life
in some manner to this world.

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:16.910
The tale of Yotsuya Kaidan
has been retold many times.

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:22.330
Could it be that the story itself
yearns to be retold?

00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:23.790
To take it a step further,

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:26.290
could it be that
the audience itself

00:18:26.380 --> 00:18:29.000
desires this curse of Oiwa
to continue?

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:34.300
Yes. Since the first reenactment
in the 8th year of the Bunsei period,

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:36.720
Tokaido Yotsuya Kaidan

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:39.560
has not simply remained a play.

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:43.940
Nor has it remained as
a fictitious story created by people.

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:46.520
It has become the basis
of the curse itself.

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:51.360
Fear has made it evolve into reality:
the true nature of the curse.

00:18:57.410 --> 00:19:00.330
You bastard, Yomoshichi.

00:19:28.360 --> 00:19:31.530
I have killed lemon
and avenged your deaths!

00:19:47.670 --> 00:19:48.920
Lady Oiwa.

00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:51.290
lemon has been punished.

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:55.220
Does this not ease
your vengeful wrath?

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:12.820
Lady Oiwa, please forgive me.

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:14.740
Even though this is merely a story,

00:20:14.820 --> 00:20:18.950
I've made you suffer
such a horrible fate.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:24.620
It's time for you
to stop cursing others.

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:27.290
If you must,
then curse me, Nanboku.

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:50.940
Let me tell you again.

00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:53.320
As to the tale of Yotsuya Kaidan,

00:20:53.360 --> 00:20:57.860
such curses only exist because
the audience desires them to.

00:20:58.240 --> 00:21:03.830
And now you have seen
all that there is to this tale.

00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:10.080
The End

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:18.920
<i>Sora wo umeru hana no iro</i>

